.SH "TypeScript"
.PP
TypeScript definitions are published via \fR\fBDefinitelyTyped\fP\fP and can be installed via the following command:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install @types/react\-transition\-group
.fi
.PP
.SH "Examples"
.PP
Clone the repo first:

.PP
.PP
.nf
git@github\&.com:reactjs/react\-transition\-group\&.git
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then run \fRnpm install\fP (or \fRyarn\fP), and finally \fRnpm run storybook\fP to start a storybook instance that you can navigate to in your browser to see the examples\&. 
